    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Corbin Carroll** stands as our highest-upside play with a stellar 85.94 score. The matchup against Adams is the primary catalyst; the park factors provide a +14% lift, and facing a pitcher with a 4.57 xERA allows **Corbin Carroll** to exploit his elite sprint speed against a favorable arm. Similarly, **Mickey Moniak** (75.98) and **James Wood** (72.52) round out our premier outfield core. **Mickey Moniak** benefits heavily from a +14% park adjustment and a +19% SP skill advantage against Kelly, while **James Wood** remains a priority start due to his elite 0.408 xwOBA and a tactical advantage against the slower delivery of Valdez, which significantly boosts his stolen base potential\u2014a critical factor for our internal weighting.\n\nThe tightest decision on the bench involved **Griffin Conine**, who posted a 48.29 score but ultimately lacked the efficiency floor provided by our starters. While **Griffin Conine** held a positive platoon edge, the combination of Gausman\u2019s 3.70 xERA and the higher-ranked projections of **Austin Riley** (66.13) and **Seiya Suzuki** (65.34) rendered him the odd man out. **Austin Riley** is a strong start today thanks to the vulnerable 5.03 xERA of Abbott, and **Seiya Suzuki**\u2019s spot in the #2 hole secures his volume in a favorable matchup against Gusto. While we are tracking the status of **Giancarlo Stanton** on the IL, the rest of the roster, including **Gabriel Moreno** and **Josh Naylor**, are cleared to capitalize on their respective SP mismatches. We continue to prioritize **Brice Turang** despite the modest penalty for the opposing catcher\u2019s pop time, as his position in the #3 order provides enough categorical cushion to offset the risk.",
